 ('EMT','Electrical metallic tubing','A raceway; verify fittings and suitability for the exposure.','electric_wiring_methods'),
 ('FAC','Flexible appliance connector','Final fuel-gas connection to an appliance; not interchangeable with CSST distribution tubing.','gas_piping'),
 ('FVIR','Flammable vapor ignition resistant','A product feature; does not by itself settle every garage installation requirement.','garage_appliances'),
 ('GFCI','Ground-fault circuit interrupter','Protection against certain ground-fault shock hazards; a successful test does not certify the whole circuit.','electric_devices'),
 ('MWBC','Multiwire branch circuit','A circuit arrangement sharing a neutral; supply legs and disconnect provisions matter.','electric_multiwire'),
 ('NM cable','Nonmetallic-sheathed cable','Cable with a nonmetallic outer sheath; check marking and application, including moisture exposure.','electric_wiring_methods'),
 ('T&P / TPR','Temperature-and-pressure relief','Relief protection with distinct temperature and pressure functions; do not confuse it with a pan drain.','water_heater_relief'),
 ('Rake / eave','Roof-edge terms','Rake: sloped edge at a gable end. Eave: lower roof edge where runoff normally leaves the plane.','roof_forms'),
 ('Grounding / bonding','Electrical connection functions','Grounding connects to earth; bonding joins conductive parts to establish the intended electrical continuity and fault-current path.','electric_service'),
 ('Gravity / forced air','Heating distribution methods','Gravity uses natural air circulation; forced air uses a blower. Neither term establishes combustion venting type.','gravity_furnaces'),
 ('COURSE / EXAM','Source flags','Training statement / recorded assessment concept. Neither alone establishes current local requirements.','inspection_method'),
 ('NOTE / LOCAL','Review flags','Reviewed explanation or correction / jurisdiction-specific qualification requiring the stated scope.','local_amendments'),
 ('Load path','Structural sequence','Route by which loads pass through connected members and bearing points to the foundation and ground.','supports'),
 ('Footing / foundation','Supporting elements','A footing spreads loads to supporting ground; the foundation transfers building loads to its support. Identify the visible assembly.','foundation_types'),
 ('Differential movement','Unequal movement','Parts of an assembly move by different amounts; crack patterns alone do not establish the cause or whether movement is active.','movement'),
 ('Capillary action','Moisture movement','Liquid movement through fine pores or narrow spaces; distinguish it from bulk runoff and vapor transport.','moisture'),
 ('Efflorescence','Mineral deposit','Surface salts left as moisture evaporates; evidence of moisture transport, not proof of an active leak at the visit.','masonry_distress'),
 ('Spalling','Surface deterioration','Flaking, breaking or loss of material at a masonry or concrete surface. Describe location and extent before assigning a cause.','masonry_distress'),
 ('Vapor retarder','Vapor-control layer','Material that limits water-vapor diffusion. Its presence alone does not establish a complete moisture-control system.','crawl_moisture'),
 ('Flood opening / air vent','Different opening functions','Flood openings address hydrostatic pressure equalization; ventilation openings address air movement. Do not use one label for both.','crawl_openings'),
 ('Joist / beam / girder','Floor support members','Joists commonly carry floor/decking loads to beams or girders; confirm actual bearing and connection, not just member size.','supports'),
 ('Bearing / connection','Load transfer','Bearing transfers load at a support surface; a connection secures or transfers forces between members. Both need context.','engineered_and_connections'),
 ('Notch / bored hole','Different member cuts','An edge cut and an enclosed hole affect a member differently; use the applicable member-specific limits.','notches_and_holes'),
 ('Cantilever','Projecting member','A member extending beyond its support. Backspan, connection and loads affect the assembly.','cantilevers_openings'),
 ('Post-tensioned slab','Prestressed concrete assembly','Tendons stressed after concrete placement; drilling or cutting can intersect concealed stressed tendons.','post_tension'),
 ('Rafter / truss','Roof framing forms','An individual sloping member versus an interconnected designed assembly. Do not apply ordinary rafter alteration assumptions to a truss.','roof_trusses'),
 ('Collar tie / rafter tie','Different tie functions','Upper ties and lower ties serve different functions and locations; identify the complete roof design.','roof_ties'),
 ('Truss uplift / rafter spread','Different movement mechanisms','Uplift is upward truss-chord movement; spread is outward movement at rafter supports. Similar finish cracks require surrounding evidence.','roof_frame'),
 ('Veneer','Nonstructural facing','A facing supported and attached to another assembly; distinguish it from structural masonry.','masonry_systems'),
 ('WRB','Water-resistive barrier','Layer within the wall water-control assembly; its continuity and integration with flashing matter.','siding_assembly'),
 ('Weep / drainage plane','Water exit and route','A weep is an opening for drainage; the drainage plane is the path behind the cladding. A visible hole does not establish the concealed path.','siding_veneer_details'),
 ('Step / counter / kick-out flashing','Roof-wall water management','Step pieces interleave with roofing; counterflashing covers an upper flashing edge; a kick-out redirects water at the lower end.','roof_flashing'),
