 ('Sash / glazing / IGU','Window parts','Sash holds glazing; an insulated glass unit combines sealed panes. Distinguish seal failure from surface condensation.','window_glazing'),
 ('U-factor / SHGC','Different window ratings','U-factor describes heat transfer; solar heat gain coefficient describes admitted solar heat. Keep units, climate and label context.','window_energy'),
 ('Ledger / guard / handrail','Deck and stair functions','Ledger transfers deck loads to a support; guard limits falls at an edge; handrail provides a graspable support.','rails_guards'),
 ('Grade / retaining wall','Site form and support','Grade is the ground slope/elevation; a retaining wall supports a difference in ground level. Trace drainage and visible movement.','retaining_wall_types'),
 ('Functional flow / drainage','Different plumbing observations','Flow concerns usable supply while fixtures operate; drainage concerns waste leaving fixtures. Record the actual test and response.','water_supply'),
 ('Cross-connection / air gap','Potable-water protection','A cross-connection can expose supply water to contamination; an air gap is a physical separation used in appropriate protection arrangements.','backflow_dwv'),
 ('Trap / vent','Waste-system functions','A trap retains a water seal; a vent manages air movement in the drainage system. Neither is a supply backflow device.','backflow_dwv'),
 ('Dielectric connection','Dissimilar-metal separation','A suitable connection limits direct electrical contact between dissimilar metals. Thread tape alone is not a listed dielectric fitting.','plumbing_materials'),
 ('Draft hood / barometric damper','Different draft devices','A gas draft hood and a swinging barometric regulator have different arrangements; match the appliance, fuel and vent system.','oil_draft'),
